  "term": "stretch receptor",
  "definition": "A stretch receptor is a sensory neuron or sensory ending that responds when tissue is stretched, producing signals that help the body detect position and movement and support motor coordination. In the source material, stretch-activated afferent neurons such as muscle spindle neurons are given as examples.",
